Package: MixOneTwoSided
Type: Package
Title: Likelihood Ratio and Bootstrap-Based Tests for Mixture of One-sided and Two-Sided Alternatives
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Anonymous", "Author",
    email = "ssbh4567@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides likelihood ratio and bootstrap-based test procedures 
             for evaluating the equality of group means against a mixture 
             of one-sided and two-sided alternative hypotheses in a one-way
             ANOVA model with unequal variances. The package implements three
             functions that perform hypothesis testing of 'H0 μ0 = μi for
             all i' against 'H1 μ0 ≤ μs (s = 1, ..., r) or μ0 ≠ μt (t = r + 1, ..., k)',
             where at least one strict inequality holds. Critical values and p-values 
             are estimated using a parametric bootstrap approach. This package is 
             particularly useful for biomedical and pharmaceutical studies where 
             treatment effects may involve both superiority (one-sided) and difference
             (two-sided) comparisons.
